      "side": 1,
      "message": "This was resolved to be an error in assembly.  PP3300_A pulls up SYS_RST_ODL via R150.  The EC\u0027s GPIO_SYS_RESET_L maps to net EC_SYS_RST_L which is in turn pulled up via D1 to SYS_RST_ODL.\n\nThis net is signaled by three different sources, each of which is on a separate power domain relative to the AP: The EC, H1, and servo connector.  Both the EC and H1 have transistor guards on their drive: D1 for the EC and Q40 for the H1.  Those guards provide open-drain logic, and allow the signal to cross the power domains.",
